{
  "_comment": "Algolia-backed sites. Each brokerage runs its own Algolia app/index with its own field names, so every site carries a full field map. Keys are the public search-only keys embedded in each site's front-end JS (safe to store). property_type is facetable on both sites (server-side filter). txn.facetable says whether the sale/lease field can be filtered server-side (Newmark: yes; RIPCO: it's a nested non-facetable field, so we filter client-side). Dotted paths (a.b) and arrays are supported by the field getter. Newmark keys: captured from nmrk.com; RIPCO: from ripcony.com. Horvath & Tremblay deferred \u2014 its listings appear to be Salesforce-backed, Algolia config not exposed client-side.",
  "sites": [
